A||||9||Doni Hagan||Steering wheel shakes?||||9||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||08-15-2001||01:46 AM||||I put shorter springs and one new front spindle on last week and ever since then the steering wheel shakes over bumps. I took care not to damage the ball joints but who knows?<P>Will a new steering stabilizer get rid of the problem or should I be looking at ball joints, tie rod ends, bearings? Get back to me as soon as you can, someone. I hate driving the car like this. ||||reg||9
Z||000001||EdsB52||08-15-2001||02:09 AM||||I'm no expert with suspensions, but I would guess that the shorter springs changed the steering geometry. It would change the camber I believe. Maybe some of the suspension experts can expound, but I would guess the camber turned inward at the top of the tire???||||reg||1
Z||000002||Doni Hagan||08-15-2001||11:06 AM||||Thanks...that makes sense. Does anyone else want to add domething?||||reg||5
Z||000003||Raydar||08-15-2001||12:55 PM||||If you put in shorter springs, they are probably stiffer as well. (Were they "cut down" stock springs?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Or aftermarket replacements?) They will transmit impacts to the wheel, instead of allowing the suspension to absorb them. They can also change the geometry, somewhat. Not sure if it'll be enough to put it out of spec, or not. The camber change may also increase steering effort and transmission of bumps. <P>If your steering stabilizer is shot, a replacement will help. Not really sure how to test it, though.<P>Many others have a lot more experience with lowered suspensions.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 08-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||hyhy4u||08-15-2001||01:31 PM||||If your wondering about your Steering Damper thats easy to check..just jack the front of the car up and take off the bolt closest to the middle..that one wont turn!..and then pull that end off the bolt.  Then see how hard it is to push in and pull back out..ususally those things are pertty stiff..hope you find out whats wrong..took me a couple months to finally solve my shaking problems!, lol  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||rogergarrison||08-15-2001||05:26 PM||||anytime you change major suspension parts you have to get a 4 wheel alignment. but dont think thats the shaking prob. did you get all the wheels on tight, or change there positions. Shaking is usually 1)bad wheel or tire 2) out of balance/round tire. try rotating your tires and see if it make anything change. You still need a 4 wheel alignment though.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52976111"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Doni Hagan||08-15-2001||08:55 PM||||Naw, I know how an "out-of-round" tire feels. This ain't it. The shaking only happens over bumps and then just long enough for the suspension to recover from the shock. I'm gonna go back and make sure everythings tight. BTW the springs were cut down one link (about .75"). Also, I know I need an alignment...It's pulling slightly to the right now and can't seem to find center. I'm really kinda sorry I did all that work just for "looks."||||reg||9
Z||000007||rogergarrison||08-15-2001||10:23 PM||||Id never cut down OEM springs myself, but thats your thing. U may have altered the spring enough that they dont sit correctly in pocket and their moving around causing the shake. Thats why if you have to lower it, recommend buying springs made for the application.||||reg||1
Z||000008||roadwarrior||08-17-2001||10:58 AM||||I'm, no suspension expert but I do understand some of the basics and by lowering the car with a suspension drop you change the suspension geometry so in turn you have some how created a situation where "bump" stear has come into play.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fierodave||08-17-2001||12:40 PM||||UMMMMM  Maybe take a look at the shocks!  lower now  and the travel on the shocks shaft is different so maybe they need to be replaced now<BR>FD||||reg||1
